,"page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#faq","content":"Yes — every call is metered under your identity and logged. Start narrow, then scale up."},"334":{"id":"/docs/ui/agents-43","page_id":"/docs/ui/agents","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/agents#faq","content":"Revoke the OAuth grant in Ambriel account settings to disconnect all sessions, or remove the connector inside the specific client."},"335":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"page","content":"Digital Footprint","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint"},"336":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-0","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","content":"See how Ambriel tracks devices, behavior and location signals to catch fake accounts and fraud before checkout completes."},"337":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-1","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#what-is-digital-footprint","content":"What is Digital Footprint?"},"338":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-2","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Signal categories"},"339":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-3","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#device-identification","content":"Device identification"},"340":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-4","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#device-safety-and-security-checks","content":"Device safety and security checks"},"341":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-5","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#email-phone-and-ip-reputation","content":"Email, phone, and IP reputation"},"342":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-6","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#real-time-location-tracking","content":"Real-time location tracking"},"343":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-7","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#network-and-connection-monitoring","content":"Network and connection monitoring"},"344":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-8","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#analyzing-software-hardware-environment-and-screen-data","content":"Analyzing software, hardware environment, and screen data"},"345":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-9","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#behavioral-and-environmental-analysis","content":"Behavioral and environmental analysis"},"346":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-10","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#geofencing-for-location-based-regulation-compliance-igaming","content":"Geofencing for location-based regulation compliance (iGaming)"},"347":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-11","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#how-is-the-fingerprint-collected","content":"How is the fingerprint collected?"},"348":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-12","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#using-footprint-data-in-decisions","content":"Using footprint data in decisions"},"349":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-13","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#faq","content":"FAQ"},"350":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-14","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#what-is-digital-footprint","content":"Digital footprint is the trail of data users leave when interacting with your product — device attributes, network details, location consistency, contact-data history, and behavior patterns. Ambriel's digital footprint capabilities turn that trail into fraud evidence by revealing patterns of online behavior, identifying suspicious activity, and verifying the authenticity of user profiles before money moves."},"351":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-15","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#what-is-digital-footprint","content":"In short: Ambriel links the device, network, contact details, and behavior of every session into one identity picture, so fakes stand out even when the name on the account looks legitimate. The signals feed the Scoring Engine and appear as evidence on each row of the Transactions queue."},"352":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-16","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#what-is-digital-footprint","content":"type: info"},"353":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-17","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#what-is-digital-footprint","content":"Footprint signals are enrichment, not verdicts. One red flag rarely decides a transaction — combine signals in scoring rules so genuine users on odd networks are not blocked by a single anomaly."},"354":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-18","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Signal"},"355":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-19","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"What it catches"},"356":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-20","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Device identification"},"357":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-21","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Multi-accounting rings and returning banned users by linking sessions across identities on the same hardware"},"358":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-22","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Device safety and security checks"},"359":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-23","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Rooted or jailbroken phones, emulators, and tampered environments used to spoof legitimate devices"},"360":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-24","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Email reputation and breach exposure"},"361":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-25","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Fake and disposable addresses, plus credentials already leaked in breaches and reused by account-takeover crews"},"362":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-26","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Phone carrier and line-type intelligence"},"363":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-27","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"VoIP burners, invalid ranges, and recently ported numbers typical of one-time abuse accounts"},"364":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-28","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"IP reputation and network analysis"},"365":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-29","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Anonymous proxies, VPN exit nodes, Tor, hosting ranges, and botnets masking the attacker's true origin"},"366":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-30","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Real-time location tracking"},"367":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-31","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Impossible travel, billing-country mismatch, and geolocation spoofing at checkout or login"},"368":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-32","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Software, hardware, and screen analysis"},"369":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-33","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Headless browsers, mismatched screen and OS fingerprints, and automation frameworks pretending to be human"},"370":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-34","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Behavioral and environmental analysis"},"371":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-35","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Bot-speed form fills, copy-paste credential stuffing, and interaction patterns no human repeats at scale"},"372":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-36","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Geofencing for regulated markets"},"373":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-37","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#signal-categories","content":"Out-of-jurisdiction play and GPS manipulation for iGaming compliance and location-gated promotions"},"374":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-38","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#device-identification","content":"Track unique devices across web and mobile platforms, linking activity across multiple sessions. When five \"different\" customers share one fingerprint, you are looking at one operator, not five buyers."},"375":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-39","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#device-safety-and-security-checks","content":"Verify the security status of a device before allowing access to your platform. This ensures that your users are legitimate and not using compromised devices such as rooted phones or emulated environments."},"376":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-40","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#email-phone-and-ip-reputation","content":"These three contact-and-network signals validate the identity anchors of an account. Disposable emails, fresh domains with no history, VoIP numbers with no tenure, and datacenter IPs each add risk weight — and together they reliably separate throwaway fraud accounts from established genuine users."},"377":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-41","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#real-time-location-tracking","content":"Track the real-time location of users, allowing you to ensure that their geolocation matches expected behavior. This is essential for spotting suspicious access attempts or potential fraud such as logins from two countries minutes apart."},"378":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-42","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#network-and-connection-monitoring","content":"Monitor the user's network and connection details to identify suspicious activity and prevent fraud, from ASN reputation to proxy and tunnel detection."},"379":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-43","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#analyzing-software-hardware-environment-and-screen-data","content":"Verify the authenticity of devices and detect potential tampering or manipulation by analyzing the software, hardware, and screen data of each user device — the inconsistencies automation leaves behind."},"380":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-44","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#behavioral-and-environmental-analysis","content":"Monitor user behavior in real time and flag deviations that could indicate fraudulent or automated activities, such as inhuman input speed or perfectly repeated interaction sequences."},"381":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-45","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#geofencing-for-location-based-regulation-compliance-igaming","content":"Integrate with real-time location tracking to validate that transactions align with local regulations, ensuring compliance while blocking suspicious attempts to manipulate location data."},"382":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-46","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#how-is-the-fingerprint-collected","content":"Collection starts with the lightweight JavaScript agent embedded on your pages — it captures device attributes, browser and screen characteristics, and behavioral telemetry during the session and attaches them to the scoring request. Follow the JS agent setup guide to install the snippet, verify events are flowing, and confirm fingerprints appear on test transactions."},"383":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-47","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#how-is-the-fingerprint-collected","content":"Native mobile SDKs provide the equivalent telemetry for iOS and Android, while server-side lookup APIs enrich email, phone, and IP fields that never touch the frontend. All three paths converge: the agent and SDKs supply what only the client can observe, the lookups add historical reputation, and the Fraud API merges everything into one footprint per transaction."},"384":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-48","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#how-is-the-fingerprint-collected","content":"type: warning"},"385":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-49","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#how-is-the-fingerprint-collected","content":"Load the agent on every page where risk matters — signup, login, and checkout — not just the payment step. Fraudsters probe early; a fingerprint captured at account creation links the later fraudulent purchase back to the same device."},"386":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-50","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#using-footprint-data-in-decisions","content":"Reference footprint fields directly in scoring rules: block datacenter IPs on high-value orders, route disposable-email signups to review, or step up authentication when device and billing country diverge. Each row in the Transactions queue shows the footprint behind its score, so reviewers see the same evidence the rules used."},"387":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-51","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#faq","content":"In most regions, device and behavior collection counts as processing that needs disclosure and often consent. Publish it in your privacy policy, wire the agent to your consent manager, and confirm the legal basis with counsel before launch."},"388":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-52","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#faq","content":"You still get a decision. The footprint is thinner — fewer device and behavior attributes — so rules should treat missing telemetry as a mild risk factor rather than an automatic block, and lean on server-side email, phone, and IP lookups."},"389":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-53","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#faq","content":"Sophisticated attackers can rotate some attributes, but rarely all of them at once across device, network, behavior, and contact history. Layered signals plus velocity tracking make large-scale evasion expensive, which is what stops most operations."},"390":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint-54","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/digital-footprint#faq","content":"Install the agent in staging per the setup guide, run a test signup and checkout, then open the matching rows in the review queue and confirm device, IP, and behavior evidence is attached before promoting to production."},"391":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"page","content":"Fraud Prevention","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention"},"392":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-0","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","content":"Stop fraud before it costs you: real-time scoring, device intelligence and rule automation for transactions across every industry."},"393":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-1","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#fraud-scoring-api","content":"Fraud scoring API"},"394":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-2","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#digital-footprint","content":"Digital footprint"},"395":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-3","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#device-intelligence","content":"Device intelligence"},"396":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-4","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#scoring-engine-and-rules","content":"Scoring engine and rules"},"397":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-5","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#transaction-review-queue","content":"Transaction review queue"},"398":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-6","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#aml-and-compliance","content":"AML and compliance"},"399":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-7","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Which product do I need?"},"400":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-8","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#products","content":"Products"},"401":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-9","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#faq","content":"FAQ"},"402":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-10","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","content":"Ambriel is a comprehensive suite of fraud prevention and compliance solutions tailored for financial services, fintechs, iGaming operators, e-commerce platforms, retailers, and other digital businesses seeking effective risk management tools."},"403":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-11","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","content":"Start here if you are new: pick the product area that matches your problem below, then follow its guide to integrate and go live. You can adopt one tool for a targeted need or combine them into a layered defense across every transaction."},"404":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-12","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#fraud-scoring-api","content":"The Fraud API is Ambriel's primary real-time decisioning endpoint. You submit transaction, customer, and session data in a single request and receive an enriched response with risk scores, triggered rules, and a recommended decision in milliseconds."},"405":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-13","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#fraud-scoring-api","content":"Use it when you need a synchronous approve-or-block answer at checkout, signup, or login. It consolidates digital footprinting, decisioning, and risk scoring into one streamlined response, so your backend makes one call instead of orchestrating five vendors."},"406":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-14","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#digital-footprint","content":"Digital Footprint reveals who is really behind a session by analyzing online behavior, device identity, location consistency, and contact-data reputation. The Email, Phone, and IP signals expose disposable addresses, breached credentials, VoIP burner numbers, and anonymized or high-risk networks before money moves."},"407":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-15","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#digital-footprint","content":"Use it when fake accounts, friendly-fraud chargebacks, or promo abuse keep slipping through. Read the Digital Footprint guide for the full signal catalog and collection setup."},"408":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-16","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#device-intelligence","content":"Device Intelligence tracks device attributes, behavioral biometrics, and interaction patterns across web and mobile sessions. By fingerprinting configurations, browser settings, and usage behavior, it exposes bots, device spoofing, emulators, and multi-accounting rings that rotate identities but reuse hardware."},"409":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-17","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#device-intelligence","content":"Use it when one attacker controls many accounts, or when automated credential stuffing and card testing spike. Pair it with velocity rules in the scoring engine to throttle repeat offenders automatically."},"410":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-18","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#scoring-engine-and-rules","content":"The Scoring Engine turns your risk policy into executable logic: custom rules over IP, customer, phone, email, BIN, and transaction attributes, combined with AND/OR/NOT operators into Approve, Review, and Reject outcomes. Analysts tune thresholds and actions without shipping code."},"411":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-19","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#scoring-engine-and-rules","content":"Use it when static vendor scores do not match your risk appetite, or when you need different policies per market, product line, or payment method. See Scoring Engine for rule types, score bands, and worked examples."},"412":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-20","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#transaction-review-queue","content":"The Transactions queue is where analysts work the output of the engine: every scored event with its decision, score, rule trace, and evidence panel in one searchable list. Triage review-band traffic, approve or overturn decisions with a recorded audit trail, and export case files for disputes and regulators."},"413":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-21","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#transaction-review-queue","content":"Use it when manual review is part of your flow, or when chargebacks demand evidence fast. The Transactions guide walks through filters, risk bands, and the daily triage routine."},"414":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-22","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#aml-and-compliance","content":"Ambriel's AML screening and monitoring tools simplify regulatory adherence while strengthening fraud detection. Watchlist and sanctions checks run alongside fraud scoring, so a single transaction view covers both financial-crime risk and compliance exposure."},"415":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-23","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#aml-and-compliance","content":"Use it when onboarding customers under KYC obligations, or when ongoing monitoring must flag sanctioned entities and suspicious patterns. These tools integrate with the Fraud API for a holistic prevention posture."},"416":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-24","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Symptom"},"417":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-25","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Product"},"418":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-26","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Start with"},"419":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-27","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Fake signups and disposable emails"},"420":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-28","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Digital Footprint"},"421":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-29","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Digital Footprint"},"422":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-30","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"One device running many accounts"},"423":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-31","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Device Intelligence"},"424":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-32","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Digital Footprint"},"425":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-33","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Need a real-time approve-or-block answer"},"426":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-34","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Fraud scoring API"},"427":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-35","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Scoring Engine"},"428":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-36","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Vendor scores don't match our risk appetite"},"429":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-37","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Scoring Engine and rules"},"430":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-38","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Scoring Engine"},"431":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-39","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Review team drowning in manual checks"},"432":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-40","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Transaction review queue"},"433":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-41","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Transactions"},"434":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-42","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Chargebacks need evidence packs"},"435":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-43","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Transaction review queue"},"436":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-44","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Transactions"},"437":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-45","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Sanctions and watchlist obligations"},"438":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-46","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"AML and compliance"},"439":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-47","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"AML Compliance"},"440":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-48","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"type: info"},"441":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-49","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#which-product-do-i-need","content":"Most teams combine at least three layers: footprint signals for enrichment, scoring rules for automated decisions, and the review queue for human oversight. Start with scoring plus one signal source, then add layers as false positives and fraud losses dictate."},"442":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-50","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#faq","content":"Individually. Each product area works standalone — for example, lookup APIs for signup validation only — and they compose into a full risk stack when you are ready. Start with your most painful fraud vector and expand from there."},"443":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-51","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#faq","content":"The Fraud API plus the JavaScript agent gives you scored transactions with device and behavior signals in days. Lookup APIs for email, phone, and IP can ship even faster since they need no frontend changes."},"444":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention-52","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/fraud-prevention#faq","content":"No — it focuses it. Automated rules clear the obvious approves and rejects so analysts spend time only on ambiguous review-band cases, with full evidence and an audit trail for every decision."},"445":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"page","content":"Scoring Engine","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine"},"446":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-0","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","content":"Learn how Ambriel scores each transaction with custom rules, score bands and decision states that approve, review or reject risk."},"447":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-1","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#scoring-engine","content":"Scoring Engine"},"448":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-2","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#how-is-the-score-calculated","content":"How is the score calculated?"},"449":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-3","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#rule-types","content":"Rule Types"},"450":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-4","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#conditions","content":"Conditions"},"451":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-5","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#actions","content":"Actions"},"452":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-6","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#what-do-score-bands-mean","content":"What do score bands mean?"},"453":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-7","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#how-do-rules-interact-with-scores","content":"How do rules interact with scores?"},"454":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-8","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#examples","content":"Examples"},"455":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-9","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"heading","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#faq","content":"FAQ"},"456":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-10","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#scoring-engine","content":"The Scoring Engine evaluates every transaction against your custom rules and produces a 0–100 risk score plus an Approve, Review, or Reject decision. Rules inspect IP, customer, phone, email, BIN, and transaction attributes, combine with logical operators, and the highest-priority match sets the outcome reviewers see in the queue."},"457":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-11","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#scoring-engine","content":"The Scoring Engine works by allowing you to define a set of rules that are evaluated for each transaction. Each rule has a set of conditions that are evaluated, and if all conditions are true, the rule is triggered. The triggered rule can then perform an action, such as setting a score, setting a state (Approve, Reject, Review), or adding a value to a list."},"458":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-12","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#how-is-the-score-calculated","content":"Each transaction runs through your rule set in priority order. Every rule whose conditions all evaluate to true fires and applies its action — setting or adjusting the score, assigning a decision state, or tagging the transaction via a list. When several rules match, the engine resolves them by priority so the most specific or most severe rule wins, and the full trace of fired rules is stored as evidence on the Transactions row."},"459":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-13","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#how-is-the-score-calculated","content":"type: info"},"460":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-14","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#how-is-the-score-calculated","content":"Scores are deterministic: the same transaction data against the same rule set always yields the same score. That makes rule changes testable — clone a rule, adjust it, and replay recent traffic before promoting."},"461":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-15","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#rule-types","content":"The following rule types are available:"},"462":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-16","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#rule-types","content":"Rule Type"},"463":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-17","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#rule-types","content":"Description"},"464":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-18","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#rule-types","content":"IP Rule"},"465":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-19","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#rule-types","content":"Evaluates the IP address of the transaction."},"466":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-20","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#rule-types","content":"Customer Rule"},"467":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-21","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#rule-types","content":"Evaluates the customer information associated with the transaction."},"468":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-22","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#rule-types","content":"Phone Rule"},"469":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-23","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#rule-types","content":"Evaluates the phone number associated with the transaction."},"470":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-24","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#rule-types","content":"Email Rule"},"471":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-25","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#rule-types","content":"Evaluates the email address associated with the transaction."},"472":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-26","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#rule-types","content":"Bin Rule"},"473":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-27","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#rule-types","content":"Evaluates the BIN (bank identification number) of the card associated with the transaction."},"474":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-28","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#rule-types","content":"Transaction Rule"},"475":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-29","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text","url":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine#rule-types","content":"Evaluates the transaction information, such as the amount or currency."},"476":{"id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine-30","page_id":"/docs/ui/fraud/scoring-engine","type":"text